    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0604" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115 C 96/151</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-23T12:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1916, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Gutierrez informs me that Pablo Lopez was brought from Santa Ysabel last
                    night and is now in penitentiary here, and that he has confessed to massacre of
                    Americans at Santa Ysabel on January 10 last.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
